\f0\fs24 \cf2 <$Scr_Ps::0>
\f1\fs22 Agent Jones arrived just as Sarah was still reeling from Kleoboulos\'92s preposterous suggestion. Circumstances deprived her of time for shock or outrage; the PAPER agent appeared, armed to the teeth and clearly up for ruining everyone\'92s evening.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
<!$Scr_Ps::0><$Scr_Ps::1>
\f1\fs22 At the sight of Sarah sharing a booth with a sweat bag in an expensive suit and three pyjama-clad old geezers, Jones instantly diagnosed a shady deal in progress. He pulled his weapon, trained it at Sarah, and shouted, \'93Freeze!\'94 Unfortunately, the karaoke was louder than any threat. And in any case, few things on this earth can interrupt an Elvis once they\'92re on stage, short of the actual fat momma singing. For the Elvi, freezing was not an option.\
A squad of PAPER agents filtered in, taking up posts by exits and in the murkier corners. Agent Jones shot a chandelier to glassy shards. Patrons ducked and scattered. In the dimmer, suddenly hostile light, it was uncertain if anyone got hit.\
With his particle pistol extended and aimed, Agent Jones scanned the room, picked out the sound booth, and adjusted the volume using angry lead. \'93EVERYONE WILL FREEZE!\'94 he commanded again, now the only voice in the club.\
Chanta rose from behind his pyramid of bottles and wobbled upright, glowering. Agent Jones spotted him at the edge of his vision\'97his neural circuits shorted for a moment. His pistol alternated mechanically, aiming first at Chanta, then Sarah. Jones nodded; agents moved in, snatching Chanta and holding him tight. Chanta kept still (bitter experience) but his eyes fizzed with rage.\
Johnny, meanwhile, had folded under the table. The Sages stood in a line with their backs to Sarah, forming the world\'92s least effective barricade: all varicose veins, arthritic joints, and shooting stars.\
Preparing for the next act, Kleo drew a slow, stately breath and stepped forward. \'93Dear, young Ajent. I wonder if you might consider, for a moment, the enormity of the storm you find yourself in.\'94\
Agent Jones briefly considered the enormity of not shooting the string-bean garden gnome where he stood, but something about the gnome knowing both his first name 
\f2\i and
\f1\i0  pronouncing it correctly gave him pause. He adjusted his red tie.\
Kleo, sensing the reptilian gearbox of Agent Jones\'92 brain in neutral, took another gliding step. \'93What are you here for, young Ajent?\'94 Again with the 
\f2\i Ah-zhant
\f1\i0 .\
Jones\'92 eyes glazed, just for an instant. Kleo flashed a beneficent smile; he\'92d been practicing beneficent smiles\'97chortles, guffaws, stares, and even snarls too\'97since Jamison Hardy was a boy.\
\'93I will have back what she took from me,\'94 Agent Jones answered, sounding like a schoolboy in front of the headmistress.\
Kleo\'92s eye twinkled, the product of much-practised beneficence. \'93What she has is neither yours nor hers.\'94\
\'93I will have the disc!\'94 Jones snapped, refocusing his aim on Kleo.\
\'93You will not have the disc,\'94 pronounced Kleo. \'93It is much too dangerous in the hands of your masters.\'94\
The percussive sound of cocking triggers and cracking knuckles rippled through the PAPER squad, every barrel now aimed at Kleo.\
\'93Then I will have her death,\'94 Agent Jones snarled.\
\'93You don\'92t want to kill her,\'94 Kleo soothed. \'93You want to please her. You want to worship her.\'94\
Chanta, inching for a better vantage, nearly swallowed his heart whole.\
Jones sagged, undone by Kleo\'92s words. Kleo tasted victory and released a gloating grin. Embarrassed by his lapse\'97he\'92d never quite mastered beneficent gloating\'97he recomposed quickly.\
Kleo might have neutralised the threat, if not for the thunderous stampede in the club\'92s depths like twenty bulls in five china shops.\
\'93What is that?\'94 Jones snapped. With a wave, he sent agents to investigate and grabbed a waiter in a chokehold, particle pistol pressed to her temple.\
Kleo shut his eyes and exhaled the breath of a professional sufferer. \'93It is the sound of several Elvi blasting all the toilets to smithereens. I strongly suggest you recall your agents.\'94\
Jones advanced, weapon raised. \'93What\'92s that you say?\'94\
The beauty of beneficent expressions is they betray no fear; Kleo radiated none. \'93Have you ever read a warranty card for an ELVIS Entertainment and Hospitality Unit? I suppose not. You\'92re too fresh to remember the emancipation of the Elvi, let alone the days when Grayling Corporation sold thousands of ELVIS clones into hospitality and domestic servitude. Pity: there\'92s one particular warranty instruction you\'92d be smart to heed.\'94\
Jones, needles of sadistic mojo returning, ground the barrel into the waiter\'92s temple. \'93Is that so? And which instruction was that?\'94\
\'93Never get an ELVIS angry.\'94\
\'93You mean these pathetic sideshow karaoke clowns?\'94\
Kleo sighed. No neutralisation tonight.\
Agent Jones had skipped THE vital rule of Ghetto ops: always assume the Elvi are packing.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl220\sb220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 <!$Scr_Ps::1><$Scr_Ps::0>
\f1\fs22 Any waiter or performer holding (which is to say, all of them) drew from somewhere on their person\'97leather jacket or sequinned jumpsuit. Against this, PAPER looked ill-prepared. An Elvis advanced on Jones. Sensing the shift, Jones put up his hands, blinking reflexively at the flood of reflected jewellery and bling\'97among them, a Star of David, a crucifix, and a shiny metallic badge. In other universes, that badge was recognised as belonging to the Bureau of Narcotics and Dangerous Drugs\'97like the one Nixon awarded Elvis in 1970.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
<!$Scr_Ps::0><$Scr_Ps::1>
\f1\fs22 \'93You should leave,\'94 said Narc Elvis.\
While Agent Jones struggled to process the stand-off and the vanishing prospect of dignified exit, one of his lieutenants stepped into the leadership vacuum. \'93Okay, okay, we\'92re leaving!\'94 he said. \'93No need to get strung out, man.\'94\
\'93What did you just say to me?\'94 Narc Elvis asked, voice cold, violence simmering.\
The agent, thinking he was bowing out on a high note, tried to walk away.\
\'93Hey!\'94 Narc Elvis grabbed his shoulder and spun him back. \'93No one ever walks out on me when I\'92m talking.\'94\
\'93Sure, sorry\'85\'94 the agent tried to pull free. \
\'93You think I\'92m strung out? You think I\'92m strung out, huh?\'94\
\'93Well, no\'97\'94\
\'93Well let me tell you, I\'92ve never been strung out in my life, except on music.\'94\
If only the agent had read the ELVIS warranty card. \'93Well, if by music you mean this karaoke shit\'97\'94\
\'93I oughta break your goddamn neck, you son of a sow. I oughta pull your goddamn tongue out by the roots. Thank you very much.\'94 With a swift karate chop to the neck, Narc Elvis sent the agent down like a sack of deep-fried pickles.\
The Elvi shot out what was left of the chandeliers and wall lights. Tourists screamed and hit the floor. In the spotlit gloom, Elvi snatched pool balls and hurled them at PAPER agents and mirrors with equal enthusiasm. Chairs splintered over the heads of anyone within reach.\
Once the Elvi launched into full bar fight mode, the PAPER agents had a snowball\'92s chance in Blue Hawaii.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl220\sb220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 <!$Scr_Ps::1><$Scr_Ps::0>
\f1\fs22 As the fight broke out, Sarah slid the disc into her bag. It glowed hot, as if her touch and the simple act of protecting it had roused it to life. For a moment, she almost dropped it to try punting it away, except a sudden conviction gripped her: losing it would be worse. There it was, glowing in her open bag, as ruddy and hale as a baby in a manger. With growing certainty, she realised it was too exposed: one quick swipe and Jones would have it. While the fight careened around her, Sarah plucked the disc from her bag and popped it into her bra. It felt exhilarating, the way the disc seemed to caress her contours.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

