\f1\fs22 Lonnie materialised at Sarah\'92s side. \'93We must get you out of here.\'94\
\'93I\'92m not leaving without Tony,\'94 Sarah said, firmly.\
By the wall, the silhouette of a figure with minor burns bounced on the balls of his feet.\
\'93Chanta?\'94 Lonnie asked, her voice inked in pathos. \'93Sugar, he\'92s\'85 not much, is he.\'94\
\'93He\'92s coming with me.\'94\
Lonnie huffed and waved another waiter to fetch Chanta. Johnny seized the moment, summoning every shred of courage to grab Lonnie by her jewel-encrusted lapels. \'93I\'92m coming with you.\'94\
Lonnie punched Johnny\'92s lights out.
